## TokenLighten MCP

TokenLighten (TL) returns exact slices + edit handles cheaply. When TL is exposed, start EVERY file task with it before Read/Grep/cat or an Explore-style subagent — above all unknown-location / multi-file discovery ("where is X", "which files", "how does X work"): Code/docs/config/logs/Office/archives=>`read_file mode=task_pack query="<verbatim request>"`+known `paths` locates and serves the frontier in one call; a pathless query may auto-narrow to one subtree (`scope_inferred`) — widen with `paths` only if the answer lies elsewhere; fan out natively only after TL reports a non-complete scope or a verified absence; never truncate/summarize. If the host reports native-bypass or exposes no TL, use native; never activate TL mid-task. `taskProfile`: user-declared `answer`=read-only,`generic`=change; never infer task-specific hints; change-task sub-questions stay `generic`/omitted. Shared workspace: every agent passes its fixed `lane`; omit when alone. Worktree: pass your own `cwd` on EVERY call; otherwise `cwd-required-for-edit`. STANDING RULE: a different task re-packs with `taskEpoch:"new"`. `task.id` outlives a restart—resend as `task_handle` to continue; stale/foreign handle refuses, recovers via `taskEpoch:"new"`. Pass `expected_state_version` ONLY beside a `task_handle`, and only a version a prior refusal reported — alone it refuses; a mismatch refuses with `retry:"new-task"` and names the live version in `actual`.

Pasted/attached docs need no reread; TL=workspace-only; use `did_you_mean`/`cwd_candidates`.

- Every reply is `{v:1,kind,...}`; `kind` alone says what you got — branch on it, not on a field's presence; absence is meaning (no `limit`=complete). The 15: `read.task_pack|text|map|batch|artifact|receipt|closure`, `search.matches|references|tree`, `edit.applied|reclassified|rolled_back|state_unknown`, `refusal`. An unrecognized `kind`=SAFE-STOP: report it, issue no edit, never infer from fields.
- Act on `decision.kind` (`read.task_pack`): `act.answer`/`act.edit`=>discovery closed; answer/edit NOW from served content, batch every ready independent concern — including independent regression-test additions — in exactly ONE `edit_file` `edits[]` call; once `prepared`, act; a read/search of UNSERVED scope is still served (cheap) — never re-pack for it; `task_pack` then refuses as `prepared-discovery-closed`. `act.edit` carries the writable `frontier`, sometimes a ready `apply`; `act.edit`+`create_target` with absent/empty `frontier`=target absent — call `edit_file create:true path=<create_target.path> content=… cwd=…` at once, no existence check. `discover`=>run its `next` (each, if several); a `gaps` `code` is SEMANTIC — no call rides it and more bytes never close one. `await_input`=>run a carried `next` first (bundle re-pack); else several `candidates` and none dominates=>`answer` task: re-pack ONCE with `read_file mode=task_pack paths=[<candidate paths>]`(+`qref` when given), never one-by-one; `generic` task: use served candidate bodies when safe, else ask. `done`=>stop. Everything else on a pack rides `plan`, starting with `evidence_model`.
- `refusal`: `code` says what failed, `retry` is the ONLY sanctioned transition. `call`=fix the named `field` (path-qualified; `did_you_mean`=near-miss, `keys`=what IS advertised) and re-issue. `challenge`=re-issue the same call with a `challenge` you author from its advertised request schema, only when new evidence changes the certified decision. `user-input`=ask. `new-task`=re-pack. `none`=this call shape is closed; `remaining`=owed work. `detail`/`candidate`/`expected_shapes`/`nearest_match` are ADVISORY — recover from them, never branch on them; on `nearest_match.out_of_range` re-issue against a covering handle, no re-read. `cause:"capped"` means truncated bytes; follow `next` (smaller scope/request), then retry. Every `next` is executable: run it verbatim, never as a template.
- `read.receipt`=your context is already current, by tag: `pack-unchanged`; `code-unchanged` (`served_by` names the earlier call that put the bytes on the wire — provenance, not a new read); `decision-unchanged` (the certified DECISION stands, not the bytes; `certified_query`=what it closed) — act on the restated certificate/frontier now; a receipt is never a re-pack cue; `kit-unchanged`; `closure-complete`. Never dead-end on a receipt: follow its `next`, or act on the evidence it restates. Lost your context (compaction/handoff)? Re-issue the SAME call with `force_serve:true` — bodies come back, receipts and pack dedup bypassed; it never returns less.
- Zoom: `evidence` items carry `body`=served now, `prior`=already in context (skip), `remaining`=unserved windows of that handle (`ranges=[..]` for several), `role`=surface. `limit`=response-level truncation; a recoverable `cause` (`wire`/`records`) ALWAYS carries `next` — run it, `source` never has one. `read.map`/`search.tree` have no range to zoom — re-request the named `symbol`/`path`; `read.artifact` addresses by `sheet`/`slides`/`pages`/`rows`/`sections`; `read.batch` entries carry their own `truncated`; known whole files=>ONE `mode=full paths=[…]`/`handles` batch; partial=>`slice`/`symbol`; `full` only for a needed small file; `mode=skeleton paths=[…]` batches skeletons, and Markdown `sections=[…]` serves at most 8 with `remaining`+executable `next`. `mode=full` past the per-task cap returns skeleton+`remaining_ranges`+a `next` — take the slice, don't retry full. Re-pack with the returned `qref`, no `query`.
- Search: `action=find query=<one identifier>`; several=>ONE `queries=[…]`, never serial; set `path` to a known package/module subtree; repo-wide only if scope is unknown; inventory=>`tree`(`scope_report.counts`=`visited|returned|excluded|errors`+reasons, `.gitignore`-honored like find; non-complete=not the whole repo); call sites=>`references`; 0-match+`absence` (or a `queries[]` term's `term_results[].status`=`absent`) means that token is verifiably/scope-complete absent, no re-grep; `references` pages via `limit`: run the returned `next` to exhaustion for full recall via `files`, never hand-build its `cursor`; `coverage_reason=candidate-list`=>run the `decision` `next` (qref+paths), never a serial `mode=full` sweep; same-task restatement auto-binds candidates.
- Edit: prepared `fast_path.kind="single-site-unique-match"` proves one edit, not an applied edit: call `edit_file` once with its `handle`/`search`/`replace`/`precondition`+`allowPathFallback:false`; no re-read/re-pack. Otherwise edit read handles, batch `edits[]`, use `unique-match`/item. A ready `change_contract` is the bounded effect area: edit only `action:"edit"` obligations by dependency stage, batch independent items; `action:"review"` is evidence, not an automatic write. New files/scratch/tests=>`create:true` with explicit `cwd` (or rooted handle); on `cwd-required-for-create`, choose from served `cwd_candidates` and resend — never native Write/Edit in-workspace; >32 KiB=fail. `edit.applied`=it landed: `core` (`counts` per FILE, not per item+`paths`)=post-edit truth, `applied`+`brace_delta`=per-file detail, `reclassification`=the answer->edit fence; `create:true`'s own `sha`/`bytes`/`total_lines`(+`applied_note`) IS the terminal proof — no read-back. `edit.rolled_back`=nothing stands; `edit.state_unknown`=disk unproven, run its `recovery` first. `operation_id` makes an edit retry safe: the same id replays the recorded outcome instead of applying twice (read tools refuse it).
- Wiring packs (`plan` `wiring`)=>write only `edit_frontier`; `mode=construct-receiver`=>follow its `next`; artifact packs need content-bearing `artifact_sections` per source.
- Archives: read via `read_file mode=archive|task_pack archive={path,member?}` + `search_files find|tree`; virtual member handles stay immutable; no native extraction. With `--allow-write` edit the outer ZIP only via `edit_file artifact={kind:"zip",members:[...]}`; tar/tar.gz/7z/rar remain read-only.
- Credentials: opaque `credentialRef`/`outputCredentialRef` only, never passwords; refs resolve from server `TOKENLIGHTEN_PASSWORD_<REF>`.
- Shell: build/tests/git only — never replace a TL-readable read with `cat`/`sed`/`rg`/native Read.
- `verifying`: after edits run tests or `diff`; a `verification` kit (tests/mocks referencing your edits, with handles) rides the edit/closure response — build harnesses from those handles (new files via `create:true`), never native reads/writes; kit bodies: `code`=served here, `served-earlier`=already in context (skip), `omitted`=NOT served (not empty)=>one batched `handles` read via its `next` — run it before your first compile/test command; `named_paths`/`missing_include_handles`=a path+handle pair, same call; `kit-unchanged`=nothing new; `verification.status:"not-applicable"`=no test/mock references the edit — nothing to verify through TL, end with the diff/test you already have. If a successful edit leaves `read.closure` open, use that closure or `next`; otherwise a passing relevant test or diff ends the task — do not call `mode=closure` ceremonially. Never retry a failed edit verbatim; once tests pass, stop — no cosmetic/whitespace polish edits.

